gfx.patch - graphics for the native build: the changes to files other work was going on in.
docs/issues/native-graphics.md says what it is and what was run.

Made against tools/recomp as it stood at the time in the line "snapshot" below.  Apply from
tools/recomp:

    cd tools/recomp && patch -p1 --dry-run < render/gfx.patch && patch -p1 < render/gfx.patch

The new files it needs are already in place and are not in the patch:
    app/gfx_rt.h  app/gfx_rt.cpp  app/settings.h
    render/layout.h  render/texpack.h  render/texpack.cpp  render/xxh3_64.h

Notes for the merge
 - hle.txt gains 16 addresses.  funcs.h changes with them, so every translation is made again and
   compiled again at its next build (about 3 minutes each).  A program that does not link
   app/gfx_rt.cpp gets the weak pass-through of hle_weak.cpp: the game as before.  They are in
   hle.txt and not in app/hle-app.txt because rta_app_orig (the unpatched translation the rig is
   compared with) must have them too.
 - app/build.py links app/gfx_rt.cpp and render/texpack.cpp into both rta_app and rta_app_orig;
   render/build.py adds texpack.cpp (it needs the Qt include flags, like backend_gl.cpp).
 - Defaults change: without options the application now runs with aspect = auto (the window's
   shape; the default window is 4:3), 4 samples, anisotropy 16, mip maps.  --plain is the picture
   as it was, for comparing with the emulator's.
 - Where this patch and the other work met (resolved here, look at them if a hunk fails):
     render/backend.h      DrawCmd: made_by / scissor_moved beside fog
     render/backend_gl.cpp the two shaders' interfaces: centroid on v_st, v_col and v_fog;
                           textureGrad in place of texture
                           a surface given back (dead_targets) also gives back its
                           multisampled buffers
     render/gs.cpp         same_state (scissor_moved and fog in one expression); the sprite's six
                           emit_vertex calls (theirs, with fog; the field shift before them);
                           end_frame (layout.flush before flush_uploads, the picture's shape at the
                           end); flush_uploads sets from_view[target.id] = false
     app/app_main.cpp      the header comment's script commands; the report at the end
     app/build.py          the job list
 - Windows: render/texpack.cpp reads PNG through QImage.  A build without Qt defines
   RTA_NO_QIMAGE (no pack; everything else works).  render/xxh3_64.h uses __uint128_t and
   __builtin_bswap64.
